abstract: >
  Glassbox is a Python toolkit for transformer language models, built on
  TransformerLens. It ranks attention heads by causal contribution with
  attribution patching (3 forward passes per analysis), selects a minimal
  circuit, and measures its faithfulness (sufficiency, comprehensiveness, F1)
  by ablation. It can draft EU AI Act Annex IV technical documentation from
  that evidence (8 of 9 sections; the Declaration of Conformity is a human
  sign-off). The repository also contains an AI-system investigation layer
  (traces, noise-aware diffs, one-factor interventions and verifiable evidence
  packages), validated so far in pre-registered experiments on small
  open-weight models. Key finding (arXiv:2603.09988): model confidence and
  explanation faithfulness are essentially uncorrelated (r = 0.009). IOI on
  GPT-2 Small, current build, default circuit: sufficiency 1.00,
  comprehensiveness 0.543, F1 0.704. Licensing: MIT core; BSL 1.1 for the
  compliance engine and the investigation layer (see NOTICE).
keywords:
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - attribution-patching
  - circuit-discovery
  - faithfulness
  - explainability
  - TransformerLens
